+## Why
+
+Some clients send partial updates as JSON Merge Patch documents, which are simpler than JSON Patch (RFC 6902). The library has no way to apply them, so each service would have to hand-roll the algorithm, including its null and `__proto__` edge cases.
+
+## What Changes
+
+- Add and export `applyMergePatch(target, patch)` from `src/index.ts`. It returns the merged document and never mutates its arguments.
+- Add a `JsonMergePatchError` for inputs that are not JSON values.
+- New capability `json-merge-patch`. No existing capability changes.
+
+**Governing standard:** JSON Merge Patch, RFC 7396 §2 (the MergePatch algorithm) and §3 (examples). The request cites RFC 7386; RFC 7396 obsoletes it and defines the same algorithm (it only corrects the media-type registration and examples), so RFC 7396 is followed, as `openspec/config.yaml` also names it. JSON values follow RFC 8259.
+
+**Breaking changes:** none; this is a purely additive export.
+
+**Out of scope:** generating a merge patch from two documents, the `application/merge-patch+json` media type and HTTP handling, and parsing JSON text (callers pass already-parsed values).
+
+## Capabilities
+
+### New Capabilities
+- `json-merge-patch`: applying a JSON Merge Patch (RFC 7396) to a JSON document, purely and safely.
+
+### Modified Capabilities
+None.
+
+## Impact
+
+- `src/index.ts`: new function and error class, reusing the existing `isObject`, `setMember` and `clone` helpers.
+- `test/merge-patch.test.ts`: new tests.
+- No new dependencies and no `package.json` change.
